(CHAPTER I) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(GENERAL OUTLINES OF THE HISTORY OF THE LABOR THEORY OF VALUE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. The following history of the labor theory of value begins with Adam) Tj T*
(Smith, not because it is supposed that Political Economy was born with) Tj T*
(the _Wealth of Nations_, but because no other work written affords so) Tj T*
(convenient a starting-point to the historian who has no desire to press) Tj T*
(his investigations into regions too remote from modern interests.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(After Adam Smith, the writers to be considered are Ricardo and Malthus,) Tj T*
(McCulloch, James Mill and Torrens, Senior, John Stuart Mill, and Cairnes.) Tj T*
(In the next great treatise after that of Cairnes, the _Principles of) Tj T*
(Economics_ of Marshall, there is nothing left of the labor theory of) Tj T*
(value, except a note at the end of a chapter on the general theory of the) Tj T*
(equilibrium of supply and demand.[1] This note, ?On Ricardo?s Theory of) Tj T*
(Value,? endeavors to state the ultimate relations of cost, utility and) Tj T*
(value in such a manner that Ricardo?s explanation of value is made to) Tj T*
(appear as a statement true as far as it goes, which errs only in being) Tj T*
(incomplete, and which is completed, not refuted, by the utility theory.) Tj T*
(This view will be taken up in the last chapter of the present essay. But) Tj T*
(no separate chapter is devoted to Professor Marshall?s work, because, as) Tj T*
(a matter of fact, the Ricardian labor theory finds no place in the text) Tj T*
(of his _Principles_. From Smith to Cairnes, the list of writers given) Tj T*
(above was selected as well calculated to exhibit the general line of) Tj T*
(development of English political economy. No attempt has been made to) Tj T*
(discover writers outside of this list, although it is not denied that) Tj T*
(such writers may not at present receive due credit for their influence) Tj T*
(upon the development of economic theory. Making no attempt at what might) Tj T*
(be called a discursive or _extensive_ study of the field, this history) Tj T*
(will be confined to an _intensive_ study of the chief writers. If it be) Tj T*
(found that certain of the above list of writers contributed nothing but) Tj T*
(error to the theory of value?and such is the case with three of them?even) Tj T*
(such a conclusion is deemed to be of historical value.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. With the limits of our field thus defined, attention should first be) Tj T*
