(called to a fairly prevalent, but mistaken, impression regarding the) Tj T*
(so-called classical labor theory of value. It is frequently assumed) Tj T*
(that this theory of value was a simple and absolute dictum, supported) Tj T*
(in substantial unanimity by a considerable body of writers, called) Tj T*
(collectively ?the classical school.? There is, no doubt, sufficient) Tj T*
(resemblance among these writers in their general tendencies of thought) Tj T*
(to justify the term ?classical school;? but with respect to their views) Tj T*
(on the central problem of value, it is their differences of opinion that) Tj T*
(at present need emphasis, just as it is these differences which take) Tj T*
(the modern reader by surprise when he first undertakes a detailed study) Tj T*
